= Module 4: Population Composition: Linguistic, Religious & Ethnic

== 4.1 Linguistic Composition of India
India is a veritable linguistic mosaic. Sir George Grierson's historic *Linguistic Survey of India (1903–1928)* identified 179 distinct languages and 544 regional dialects. In modern India, the Constitution recognizes *22 Scheduled Languages* under the Eighth Schedule.

